{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently underestimates prices by 5-10 EUR when the market is in an uptrend or recovering from lows, failing to capture the magnitude of upward spikes.",
    "Eliminate excessive mean reversion: The model forecasts a slow, monotonic drift toward a static mean (approx. 68-72 EUR) regardless of recent volatility; adjust forecasts to reflect the actual higher volatility range (70-76 EUR) observed in the true data.",
    "Reduce lag on sentiment shifts: When sentiment history shows consecutive high values (1.00), the model reacts too slowly to price increases; apply an immediate upward adjustment to the first 5-10 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "Avoid overshoot dampening: The model fails to sustain high prices after a spike (e.g., dropping from 76 to 70 too quickly); extend the duration of elevated price levels in the forecast to match the persistence seen in the true outcomes.",
    "Horizon-specific adjustment: The error is most pronounced in the first 10 days of the 30-day horizon; apply a larger positive correction factor for the near-term forecast compared to the long-term tail."
  ]
}
